linux/
kosmos-kernel-pkg/
kosmos-kernel-*.tar.gz
*.o

# Running gr-kosmos's unit tests produces these. They only started appearing
# once there were tests that could actually be run off the Pi.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Update-signing key material (4d). make-keys.sh already REFUSES to write
# inside the work tree, so nothing should ever match these -- they are the
# second lock, for a key that arrives some other way: copied here by hand to
# "just test something", or dropped in by a script that took a wrong path.
#
# A private key pushed to a public repo is compromised the moment it lands and
# rewriting history does not un-publish it, so the cost of the redundant rule
# is nothing and the cost of not having it is a new CA and a reflash of every
# box in the field.
*.key.pem
*.key
*.pem
